v2-bootstrap: separate the start expression from the step guards (PATCH 8)

Comment-only, one file (dag/gunbc/parse_verdict_restore.dag), 0 non-comment lines
changed; PATCH 7 (bda8255e415, tree 96103c723b4c) preserved.

PATCH 7 asserted that merge_group and workflow_dispatch "name no start at all, where
every ordinal is a typed miss and the walk is a full walk". That does not follow from
the expression: on those triggers the locate step never runs, because its own guard
skips it, so the outcome is a skipped step, not typed misses, and no walk runs to be
full or partial. An empty-expression case and a guarded-skip case were conflated.

The comment now says only what the source shows: parse_verdict_ancestor_base_sha_expr
names the start (github.event.pull_request.base.sha on pull_request, otherwise
github.event.before), while whether these steps run at all is decided separately by
the guards on the steps -- the emitted locate step and the reuse walk both run under
github.event_name == 'pull_request', the publish walk under github.event_name ==
'push' && github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' -- and it makes no claim about triggers
whose guards skip them. No claim of execution.
